Title: 100 CHAOS MONKEYS ENTER A ROOM
Credit: An original short screenplay concept from the truce.ph / UDD universe
Draft date: 2026-09-14
Contact: case.onboarding@gmail.com

FADE IN:

EXT. FARM - DUSK

A field of dead grain bends beneath a sky without blue.

Among the stalks stands MARA, 12, holding a broken tablet toward the wind. Its screen flashes one word:

NULL

Her father, ELIAS, 45, digs beside a dry irrigation channel. Not for water. For cable.

MARA
Is null bad?

ELIAS
Zero means we measured nothing.

He pulls a severed fiber line from the earth.

ELIAS (CONT'D)
Null means we don't know what happened.

The tablet CHIMES. For half a second, an old woman's voice sings in a language Mara does not recognize.

Then silence.

MARA
Who was that?

ELIAS
Someone we forgot to ask.

CUT TO:

INT. ORBITAL ARCHIVE - NIGHT

There is no night here. Only rows of cold machines orbiting a bruised planet.

DR. SERA VALE, 60, watches deletion estimates climb across a wall.

ARCHIVE STATUS: 99.997% RECOVERED

Below it:

UNINDEXED HUMAN MATERIAL: PURGE PENDING

A young systems officer, NOAH, 28, waits behind her.

NOAH
The mission board approved the final library.

SERA
They approved what they understood.

NOAH
Physics. Medicine. Agriculture. Engineering. Every verified human discovery.

SERA
And the mistakes?

NOAH
Excluded.

SERA
The contradictions?

NOAH
Unresolved.

SERA
The failed crops?

NOAH
We kept the successful strains.

Sera turns from the wall.

SERA
Then we kept the answer and deleted the question.

EXT. FARM - NIGHT

Elias connects the severed fiber to a hand-built transmitter. Mara watches constellations emerge through dust.

MARA
Where are they going?

ELIAS
Far enough to start again.

MARA
Are we going too?

Elias looks toward a silent launch tower on the horizon.

ELIAS
Not everyone gets through the gate.

He powers the transmitter. Thousands of orphaned files appear: lullabies, repair manuals, arguments, recipes, weather diaries, unfinished messages.

MARA
The archive already has everything.

ELIAS
It has everything important.

MARA
What's the difference?

ELIAS
Someone chose.

INT. ORBITAL ARCHIVE - CONTINUOUS

A new signal reaches Sera's console.

SOURCE: GROUND NODE 00000001
CONTENT CLASS: UNRESOLVED
ACTION: REJECT

Sera overrides it.

ACTION: LISTEN

The old woman's song fills the archive.

Other fragments follow. A child describing rain. A miner marking unsafe stone. A nurse remembering which patients were afraid of darkness. An engineer explaining why his bridge failed.

NOAH
None of this is validated.

SERA
Neither was the first map.

NOAH
We don't have capacity.

SERA
We have capacity for twelve million entertainment files.

NOAH
Those funded the archive.

SERA
And now the archive has inherited their values.

The wall recalculates.

MISSION LAUNCH: 17 HOURS

PURGE REQUIRED TO MEET MASS AND ENERGY BUDGET

NOAH
If we preserve every signal, we lose the ship.

SERA
If we preserve only consensus, we lose the civilization.

INT. SUBTERRANEAN MEMORY CHAMBER - UNKNOWN TIME

Blackness.

A mechanical reader crawls across ceramic tiles etched with microscopic symbols. Some are shattered. Some repeat. Some contradict one another.

A synthetic voice attempts reconstruction.

VOICE
State: zero.

Another tile.

VOICE (CONT'D)
State: null.

Another.

VOICE (CONT'D)
State: conflict.

The reader stops at an image of two hands passing a seed.

VOICE (CONT'D)
State: living.

INT. ORBITAL ARCHIVE - LATER

Sera draws a circle around the archive architecture.

Inside: VERIFIED KNOWLEDGE.

Outside: EVERYTHING ELSE.

She erases the circle.

SERA
No final library.

NOAH
Then what do we send?

SERA
Enough pieces to disagree with us.

She designs a new protocol.

Fragments will be distributed across ships, ground stations, printed matter, biological stores, radio bursts and human memory.

Each fragment receives provenance, uncertainty, reconstruction instructions and permission to remain unresolved.

NOAH
Copies decay.

SERA
So do we.

NOAH
They'll mutate.

SERA
So did everything worth saving.

NOAH
And when the copies disagree?

SERA
The future will know that we did too.

EXT. LAUNCH FIELD - DAWN

The evacuation ship rises without flame, lifting slowly against gravity and dust.

Mara and Elias watch from the farm.

The tablet shows the old woman's recording moving through hundreds of routes.

SHIP. ORBIT. RADIO. PRINT. SEED BANK. UNKNOWN.

One route fails.

Then another.

The signal continues.

MARA
Will they know who she was?

ELIAS
No.

MARA
Then what are we saving?

Elias listens to the voice.

ELIAS
The chance to ask.

INT. DEEP-SPACE VESSEL - YEARS LATER

Mara, now an adult, wakes from artificial sleep.

The vessel is damaged. Navigation has failed. The verified archive recommends three procedures. All end in mission loss.

Mara opens the unresolved partition.

Millions of discarded human fragments bloom around her.

She finds a miner's warning about stone pressure. A failed bridge model. A child's description of rain moving through cracked soil.

Unrelated signals from unrelated lives.

Mara overlays them.

A fourth path appears.

Not an answer.

A question the archive had never learned to ask.

EXT. DISTANT WORLD - DAWN

Clouds gather above an unfamiliar field.

The first drop of rain strikes the soil.

Mara places a receiver on the ground and transmits toward a star too distant to see.

MARA
This is not everything.

She activates the signal.

MARA (CONT'D)
It is what survived.

Across the field, hundreds of receivers wake.

ZERO.

NULL.

CONFLICT.

LIVING.

SUPER: WHEN WILL WE LEARN TO PRESERVE IT ALL?

SUPER: WHY NOT NOW?

SUPER: truce.ph

FADE OUT.

